<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Aug - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Aug - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-August 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-August 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over January-August 1995 and their January-August 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  (1) Memphis		1,246,435 tonnes  up 10.5pct</p>
<p> 2  (4) Los Angeles	  1,105,921 tonnes  up    8.5</p>
<p> 3  (5) Miami		  1,104,323 tonnes  up    9.1</p>
<p> 4  (3) New York	     1,052,757 tonnes  up    1.4</p>
<p> 5  (2) Tokyo		  1,035,105 tonnes  down  5.2</p>
<p> 6  (7) Hong Kong		984,207 tonnes  up    4.7</p>
<p> 7  (6) Frankfurt		966,151 tonnes  up    2.0</p>
<p> 8  (8) Louisville	     909,973 tonnes  up    2.6</p>
<p> 9 (10) Seoul		    853,438 tonnes  up    9.4</p>
<p> 10(15) Anchorage		826,632 tonnes  up   33.7</p>
<p> 11 (9) Chicago		  801,207 tonnes  down  0.2</p>
<p> 12(12) Singapore		771,608 tonnes  up    5.6</p>
<p> 13(11) London Heathrow	742,918 tonnes  up    1.2</p>
<p> 14(13) Amsterdam		720,639 tonnes  up   10.9</p>
<p> 15(16) Paris-CDG		631,582 tonnes  up    3.2</p>
<p> 16(14) New York Newark	630,609 tonnes  up    1.2</p>
<p> 17(17) Atlanta		  522,094 tonnes  up    3.7</p>
<p> 18(18) Dallas Fort Worth    500,908 tonnes	  0.0</p>
<p> 19(19) Taipei		   496,445 tonnes  up    0.4</p>
<p> 20(-)  Dayton		   476,257 tonnes  up   18.3</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
